nd in equation (REF ) indicates that {{formula:b636f60e-37ab-4108-a13b-e19d22713f38}}which indicates that the inequality (REF ) holds for {{formula:e8eb9749-a031-43b4-ad84-45af2f80ad1d}} . When {{formula:77c8e781-dcc1-434b-a910-ee8169719f14}} , the bound in equation (REF ) leads to {{formula:846d3167-1208-46b0-82b2-ef791b4a85a8}}As long as we can choose {{formula:4f25b070-2d7b-48e5-9381-530675648d95}} and {{formula:3975acb4-d43a-4d81-a439-59fbc8aee27c}} such that {{formula:0f193520-7c3e-4516-8be0-ba2983903909}} , then the inequality in the above display becomes {{formula:af5f733b-5d0c-4939-b901-ca2bcfa5220b}}Since {{formula:fe28a71e-2cda-4777-8eeb-96d229575b7c}} for all {{formula:6182fcd0-c290-4cf7-8f97-dcf60fcfe35c}} , the inequality {{formula:e695abf4-2499-4795-8d3b-7f5a74a4326d}} holds as long as {{formula:085c48b3-e3c9-48d4-a657-937532f37184}} , which is valid based on our hypothesis. As a consequence, we obtain the conclusion of the induction argument.Now, we would like to upper bound {{formula:23d7c5d4-101f-4dbc-9fbc-129f608a639a}} when {{formula:a1bf4fbd-cec4-4e73-b9b1-f35286c5d416}} . Indeed, from the formulation of {{formula:f34f2525-46d5-4c7e-a789-2d7ed80d81b9}} , we have {{formula:ecee7b64-bf5e-4ae8-93f5-4af5a0287843}}Since {{formula:f7842274-c9ff-4cd8-881f-c9fc19593122}} is a concave function in the domain {{formula:841238e8-a131-4f11-87aa-f249ccc6eaaf}} , an application of Jensen inequality leads to {{formula:aa375e1d-ce04-4ead-bf38-3f943c57c9dd}}where the final inequality is due to {{formula:ef304edc-b7cf-47d3-8d7c-e740e3f9949e}} , which indicates that {{formula:06e9d627-a54d-4b51-8674-e289297a2a64}} . Collecting these results, we obtain that {{formula:6ae6dc8e-93ae-48c2-8f21-3b664ab1da94}}Given the bound in equation (REF ), the condition {{formula:8d7af061-f6e6-4b63-994f-7f86a305f15c}} before equation (REF ) is satisfied as long as {{formula:e32145d2-e57d-41b1-bf8c-c32419484c54}} , which is equivalent to {{formula:3713c04b-fb63-4914-a3b5-9fe77e7a8552}